A viable route exists, so I’m not rejecting it: this is a native Track B cryptogram family. The instance will keep the paper’s ciphertext-only task, add only a SHA-256 plaintext commitment for exact grading, and vary difficulty by hiding more of the inverse permutation (then shortening context), so the 26-letter witness stays fixed while the search space grows.
